 "_coverage": "369 of 369 members — COMPLETE. The capture reached every member of the collection.",
 "_why_this_matters": "California license titles track occupational titles, so they join to kb/reference/coe_occupation_demand_2024_2029.json by name far better than the national certification collection does. These are also the credentials a California student actually holds, which is what a CPL conversation turns on.",
 "_cpl_caveat": "A license is an occupational gate. CPL awards credit for the training and experience behind it. A license on this list signals that a student completed something a college can assess; the college still decides what credit that training carries. Treat a license as evidence to pursue, and let a faculty ruling set the award.",
 "_no_occupation_field": "The collection list view carries the credential name and the issuing agency. It omits ceterms:occupationType and the O*NET-SOC code, so a name join or a curator ruling is what connects these to an occupation. Sam confirmed on 2026-09-16 that the page offers no download or export control.",
 "_network": "credentialengineregistry.org and credentialfinder.org are BLOCKED by this network's egress policy (connect_rejected, verified 2026-09-16 via curl and WebFetch). A human-captured page is the channel.",
