 "_join_measured_2026_09_16": "Joined by name to the 541 COE occupations with Matcher from kb/_build_regional_cpl_opportunity.py: 73 occupations matched (13%), 115 occupation-license pairs. Good hits include Heating, Air Conditioning and Refrigeration Mechanics -> Warm-Air Heating, Ventilating and Air-Conditioning Contractor, and Barbers -> Barber.",
 "_matcher_defect_found": "OVER-STEMMING ON AGENT SUFFIXES. stem() strips -er/-ors/-or when the token is longer than 4 characters, so 'engineer' reduces to 'engine' and 'actor' reduces to 'act'. That produced 8 false pairs resting on the engine/engineer collapse alone (Bus and Truck Mechanics and Diesel Engine Specialists -> Engineer In Training) and one on act/actor (Actors -> California Residential Mortgage Lending Act). The plural suffixes are safe; the agent suffixes collide with real words. A fix protects a token whose stem is itself a literal token in either corpus. UNFIXED as of 2026-09-16 -- the same matcher drives the regional opportunity build, so the change needs its own run and a look at what moves.",
 "_detail_page_print": "Sam printed one detail page on 2026-09-16 (the NICE Framework work role Secure Systems Development, CTID ce-0729ead7-6586-4020-895e-0990b0a84221). The print carries the full record: 73 Task statements, each with its own CTID, plus Knowledge and Skill statements. It carries no occupation code either. For CPL that task list is the more useful half -- faculty map credit against learning outcomes, which is what Phase 4 (SLO ingestion) in the roadmap is for. Printing 369 detail pages one at a time stays impractical, so the detail print fits a credential a college is actually pursuing."
}